<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Laguna de Bay</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Laguna de Bay is the largest lake in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippines">Philippines</a>, lying south-east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manila">Manila</a> on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luzon">Luzon</a> and draining into Manila Bay through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pasig-river">Pasig River</a>. Before Spanish rule its shores were settled by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tagalog-language">Tagalog</a> communities that farmed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rice">rice</a>, fished and traded with Chinese merchants. Some scholars place the early trading polity of Ma-i at Bay on its southern shore.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/laguna-de-bay.jpg" alt="Laguna de Bay" width="320" height="233" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Provided by the ISS Crew Earth Observations Facility and the Earth Science and Remote Sensing Unit, Johnson Space Cen... · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Laguna_de_Bay_2020_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
